<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>
  <!-- Ash'karr's river steam, wired as DATA (MANYWATERS_GENERIC_SPLIT_1).

       ManyWaters (merged into mandrake.rm.flowworks 2026-09-16) is a RimMandrake-tier generic
       water-effects engine, so it names no biome of its own. Until this patch
       existed, MapComponent_RiverSteam gated on the literal string
       "ZBiome_Grasslands" inside the engine's C# — backwards: which biome
       steams is campaign wiring, and campaign wiring lives here.

       RM_FE_Pyrelands (mandrake.rm.pyrelands) is the Pyrelands biome the frozen
       world actually carries — 222 tiles, MEASURED live 2026-09-19. The second
       operation below is the one that does the work on the shipped world.
       ZBiome_Grasslands is zylle's More Vanilla Biomes grassland, still labelled
       "the Pyrelands" by BiomeNames_Ashkarr.xml but carrying ZERO tiles on the
       canonical planet; it is patched too, conditionally, and costs nothing.

       ⚠️ Gated twice, both deliberately:
       - PatchOperationFindMod on ManyWaters, because a `Class=` naming a type
         no loaded assembly has DISCARDS THE WHOLE BiomeDef, silently, and
         takes every biome in that file with it. If ManyWaters is cut, this
         must be a no-op, not a dead grassland.
       - PatchOperationConditional on the def itself, because
         ZBiome_Grasslands comes from a third-party mod that may not be
         active; a bare Add against a missing xpath is a patch error.

       🔑 REFACTOR, NOT A FEATURE CHANGE. Every field on
       RiverSteamBiomeExtension defaults to the value the engine used while
       the biome was hardcoded (Steam fleck, 90~260 tick gap, 1~1.8 scale,
       60~120 deg, 0.15~0.3 speed), so this empty declaration reproduces the
       old behaviour exactly. Override a field here — never in the engine — if
       the Pyrelands should ever steam differently from anywhere else. -->

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
    <mods>
      <!-- Merged into FlowWorks 2026-09-16 (FLOWWORKS_BUILD_PROGRAM_1 Phase 1).
           PatchOperationFindMod matches ModLister.HasActiveModWithName - the mod's
           <name>, never its packageId - so this string must track the About.xml
           name exactly, and a stale one no-ops the whole wiring in silence. -->
      <li>RimMandrake: FlowWorks</li>
    </mods>
    <match Class="PatchOperationConditional">
      <xpath>/Defs/BiomeDef[defName="ZBiome_Grasslands"]</xpath>
      <match Class="PatchOperationConditional">
        <!-- Checked against More Vanilla Biomes 1.6's own
             Defs/BiomeDefs/ZBiome_Grasslands.xml, 2026-09-08: no
             <modExtensions> there, so the nomatch branch is the live one.
             The match branch exists because a SECOND <modExtensions> element
             on one def is not a merge — the loader reads one and the other's
             contents are silently gone. -->
        <xpath>/Defs/BiomeDef[defName="ZBiome_Grasslands"]/modExtensions</xpath>
        <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>/Defs/BiomeDef[defName="ZBiome_Grasslands"]/modExtensions</xpath>
          <value>
            <li Class="RimMandrake.FlowWorks.ManyWaters.RiverSteamBiomeExtension" />
          </value>
        </match>
        <nomatch Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>/Defs/BiomeDef[defName="ZBiome_Grasslands"]</xpath>
          <value>
            <modExtensions>
              <li Class="RimMandrake.FlowWorks.ManyWaters.RiverSteamBiomeExtension" />
            </modExtensions>
          </value>
        </nomatch>
      </match>
    </match>
  </Operation>


  <!-- 🔴 RM_FE_Pyrelands is the biome the FROZEN WORLD actually carries.
       MEASURED live 2026-09-19 (FOUNDRY bridge wave 2) against the canonical
       planet (seed "raven", coverage 1.0, jawa/world_tile_export, 21872
       surface tiles): 222 tiles are BiomeDef RM_FE_Pyrelands and ZERO are
       ZBiome_Grasslands. The Pyrelands moved off zylle's reskinned grassland
       onto our own biome def in mandrake.rm.pyrelands, and the operation above
       was never re-pointed — so on the shipped world MapComponent_RiverSteam
       could never fire on a single tile, and the item's "steam has never been
       seen" symptom had this as its cause, not a render bug.

       Both defNames are patched, not one: ZBiome_Grasslands is still labelled
       "the Pyrelands" live and may carry tiles on a non-canonical world, and
       every operation here is conditional on the def existing, so patching a
       biome with no tiles costs nothing. -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
    <mods>
      <li>RimMandrake: FlowWorks</li>
    </mods>
    <match Class="PatchOperationConditional">
      <xpath>/Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RM_FE_Pyrelands"]</xpath>
      <match Class="PatchOperationConditional">
        <xpath>/Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RM_FE_Pyrelands"]/modExtensions</xpath>
        <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>/Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RM_FE_Pyrelands"]/modExtensions</xpath>
          <value>
            <li Class="RimMandrake.FlowWorks.ManyWaters.RiverSteamBiomeExtension" />
          </value>
        </match>
        <nomatch Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>/Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RM_FE_Pyrelands"]</xpath>
          <value>
            <modExtensions>
              <li Class="RimMandrake.FlowWorks.ManyWaters.RiverSteamBiomeExtension" />
            </modExtensions>
          </value>
        </nomatch>
      </match>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
